course: dictionary
lesson: 5211
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things. Jasper is a boy's name, but it is also a hard stone. Context tells you which one is meant. «In Toronto, kids ask Jasper to buy them snacks every day, and he does.» Here Jasper is someone who buys snacks, so it is a person's name.
explain: Look at the capital letter. A capital letter at the start of a word often marks a name of a person, a place or a special thing. Jasper with a capital J is a name. Jasper with a small j, as in «red jasper», is a common word for a stone.
explain: Always ask: what would fit in this sentence? Try your meaning in place of the word. If you read «He gave her a red jasper», a stone makes sense. If you read «Jasper gave her a red stone», a person makes sense. Checking like this stops you choosing the wrong meaning.
fact: Jasper is a hard stone, usually red, yellow, brown or green, often with patterns.
fact: People polish jasper to make jewellery and ornaments.
fact: Jasper is also a boy's name, written with a capital J.
fact: Jasper is a town and national park in the Rocky Mountains of Canada.
fact: Jasperware is a kind of pottery, usually pale blue with white raised pictures, made by the Wedgwood company.
exercise: «In Toronto, kids ask Jasper to buy them snacks every day, and he does.» In this sentence, what is Jasper? | A kind of pottery | *A boy's name | A town in Canada | A hard, coloured stone
exercise: Read «red jasper». What is jasper here? | A blue plate with white pictures | *A hard stone, often with patterns | A mountain in Canada | A boy who lives in Toronto
exercise: Why does Jasper start with a capital J in «Jasper is my cousin»? | *It is a name | It is the start of a song title | It is a stone | It is the first word of a question
test: «She wore a ring with a polished piece of jasper.» What is jasper here? | A national park | *A hard stone, polished for jewellery | A kind of paint | A boy's name
test: «Jasper lives next door and walks his dog every morning.» What does the capital J tell you? | *Jasper is a person's name | Jasper is a rule for spelling | Jasper is a hard stone | Jasper is a colour
exam: Read «Jasper gave Mia a red stone with patterns.» Is Jasper a name or a stone here, and how do you know? | A name, because there is a red word in the sentence | A stone, because the sentence has a stone in it | A stone, because stones are red | *A name, because the capital J and the person doing the giving
